diff --git a/crates/rightkit-credentials/CHANGELOG.md b/crates/rightkit-credentials/CHANGELOG.md
index 49bf664..3ed8437 100644
--- a/crates/rightkit-credentials/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/crates/rightkit-credentials/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -1,5 +1,21 @@
 # Changelog
 
+## 0.2.2 (unreleased)
+
+Additive only (new modules, functions and types; no existing item changes), so a patch release. Written without a compiler run on any host: nothing below has been built or tested yet. Hard rule (rightkit#771 D4): no credential is written to a plain file by anything in this crate.
+
+- Added (rightkit#458): feature `env-file` (off by default, headless daemons only; adds `rightkit-fs`): `secret_from_env_file(var)`, `secret_from_env_file_with(var, env)`, `secret_from_file_named(var, path)`, `SecretFileError` (`NotSet`, `Missing`, `Unsafe`, `TooLarge`, `Empty`, `Io`; converts into `Error`) and `MAX_SECRET_FILE_BYTES` (64 KiB). Reads the secret from the file named by an environment variable and fails closed: a symlink or non-regular file, a file over the limit, a file not owned by the user or not owner-only (`rightkit_fs::private::verify_owner_only`: Unix mode and macOS ACL, Windows owner and DACL), or one empty after trimming is refused. The owner-only check runs before and after the read; the buffer is wiped; no error carries the value. The module only reads (a source-scan test pins that it contains no file-writing call).
+- Added (rightkit#749): `AppleHelper::new_trusted(path, HelperTrust) -> Result<AppleHelper>` and `AppleHelper::with_trust`, with the `apple_trust` module (`HelperTrust`, `TeamPolicy::{SameAsHost, Fixed, Skip}`, `contain_in_bundle`). The helper path is canonicalized and must be a regular file strictly inside the app bundle; on macOS it must also pass a strict static validity check (`SecStaticCode`, falling back to `/usr/bin/codesign`) and carry the required Team ID (`anchor apple generic and certificate leaf[subject.OU]`). For a main executable of an `.app` the whole `.app` is checked. Re-checked before every spawn; the canonical path runs. Unsigned, ad-hoc, foreign-signed or unrunnable-check is a refusal; off macOS a signature policy other than `Skip` is refused. `AppleHelper::new` is unchanged and still checks nothing. Limit: a process that can replace files in the install directory can replace the host executable too, and the check-to-exec gap is narrowed, not closed.
+- Added (rightkit#698): `apple_helper::resolve_bundled_login_item(name)` (the nested `Contents/Library/LoginItems/<name>.app/Contents/MacOS/<name>` layout, canonical, regular file, contained in the bundle) and `apple_helper::LoginItemLookup` with the opt-in `dev_fallback(true)`: for an executable that is NOT inside an `.app`, a bare `<name>` file next to it or in its parent directory (canonical, regular, contained in that directory). Never used inside a bundle.
+- Added (rightkit#410): blob sealing. `Sealer` (`StoreKey`: AES-256-GCM under a 256-bit key kept in the credential store, so Keychain-wrapped on macOS; `Dpapi`: Windows `CryptProtectData`/`CryptUnprotectData`, user scope, never prompting), `seal_blob`/`open_blob`/`is_sealed` (`magic | body`), `aead_seal`/`aead_open`, `dpapi_protect`/`dpapi_unprotect` (Windows only, `Error::Unavailable` elsewhere), `seal_mac`/`check_mac` (HMAC-SHA-256, hex, constant time), `to_hex`/`from_hex`. Only ciphertext is ever written by a caller; the key is in the credential store.
+- Added (rightkit#410): PIN-derived keys. `derive_pin_key` (PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA-256, 310,000 rounds), `wrap_key`/`unwrap_key`, and `PinSealKey`: the HMAC seal key of a stored blob kept as ONE CREDENTIAL-STORE ITEM (never a file), wrapped under the owner's PIN once one is set (`make_seal`, `check_seal`, `pin_entered`, `pin_changed`, `pin_bound`, `key_from_pin`, `reset`). A clear or planted key is never adopted when the PIN is entered, a store failure is never read as absence, and a damaged item is never overwritten by a first-run mint. This replaces the earlier draft's file-backed `SealKeyFile` (a clear mode-0600 key file off Windows), which conflicts with rightkit#771 D4 and is not provided.
+- Added (rightkit#410): macOS keychain partition-list verification. `PartitionPolicy::team(<team id>)`, `judge_partitions`, `partition_tokens_from_description` (all platforms, unit-tested) and, on macOS, `verify_login_keychain_item` and `read_login_keychain_item`: the item is found in the login keychain only (path from the account database; the default keychain must be the login keychain), its partition list must be exactly the team's, checked before and after a never-prompting read. Shares the process-wide keychain UI lock with the `Store` backend. Defence in depth, not a boundary.
+- Added (rightkit#410): user verification. `verify_user`, `verify_user_for_window`, `verification_availability`, `VerifyOutcome`, `VerifyAvailability`. Windows Hello through `UserConsentVerifier`, behind the new off-by-default `windows-hello` feature (adds `windows` 0.62 and `windows-future` 0.3, Windows only). Only a `Verified` result is a pass; every other result is `Cancelled`, `NotVerified` or `Error::Unavailable`. Everywhere else `Error::Unavailable`; on macOS use RightKitSwift `UserVerification` (LocalAuthentication has no C API).
+- Added (rightkit#410): `verify_p256`, `owner_key_id` and `P256_PUBLIC_KEY_LEN`, the Rust verify side of an owner approval signed by the Secure Enclave key in RightKitSwift `OwnerKey` (raw 64-byte or DER ECDSA P-256 / SHA-256 over a 65-byte X9.63 point).
+- Dependencies: `ring` 0.17 (all platforms), `libc` 0.2 (macOS only), `rightkit-fs` 0.4.3 (optional, feature `env-file`), `windows` 0.62 and `windows-future` 0.3 (optional, Windows, feature `windows-hello`).
+- Not delivered (rightkit#410): a TPM-backed signing key on Windows (needs a Windows machine with a TPM to design and test; Windows Hello `KeyCredential` is RSA and would need its own verify path), and the Secure Enclave signing key and Touch ID, which are Swift (RightKitSwift, the Mac owner's lane). The earlier draft's HMAC `approval-tokens` feature (GenRight approval primitive) is not included: no open issue asks for it.
+- Tests: unit tests cover the platform-independent logic (AEAD, base64, hex, MAC, PIN wrap, `PinSealKey` over the in-memory store, partition parsing and policy, outcome mapping, P-256 verify, bundle containment, login-item lookup, secret-file rules); `tests/seal.rs` the public surface; `tests/secret_file_feature.rs` and `tests/no_credential_files.rs` pin the feature gating and that no module writes a file. Not run: DPAPI, Windows Hello, the keychain partition read and the macOS signature check need Windows or macOS hardware.
+
 ## 0.2.1 (2026-10-17)
 
 - Added (rightkit#509): `Store::generate_key(bytes) -> Result<Secret>`, a public fresh-key generator (OS CSPRNG, standard base64 text, 16..=1024 bytes, nothing stored) for rotation keys; `get_or_create_key` now uses it. Additive.
